Clinical terminologies are not part of this distribution

HealthCraft's code is open source. Several clinical code systems it can use are not, and none of
their content is in this repository:

- CPT® is owned by the American Medical Association and needs a license from the AMA.
- SNOMED CT is licensed through SNOMED International (free in member countries such as the US via
  the UMLS Metathesaurus License); it may not be redistributed here.
- Commercial drug knowledge bases (for example First Databank, Medi-Span) are licensed by their
  vendors.
- LOINC, RxNorm and ICD-10-CM are available without fee under their own terms; their files are
  still loaded at deployment time rather than bundled.

Each deployment loads the terminology files it is licensed to use (see
crates/terminology/README.md).

Not a medical device

HealthCraft is pre-release software under active development. It is not certified health IT
(ONC/ASTP), not cleared by the FDA or any other regulator, and must not be used to make clinical
decisions or to store real patient data. Use synthetic data only.
